  "title": "Mattox and Hudson work-from-home booklet assembly scheme",
  "typology": "job-scam",
  "period": "to 2012",
  "summary": "A federal grand jury in the Northern District of Georgia indicted Detrick Mattox and Jasmine Hudson of Ellenwood, Georgia, for a work-from-home scheme run under at least 14 business names. Internet ads promised earnings of up to $5,000 a week assembling booklets; more than 200 people paid initiation fees of $50 to $500, most received no materials, and those who did the work were never paid. The August 2012 announcement reports charges only; indictments are allegations, and no outcome was verified.",
